{"items": [{"owner": {"account_id": 5171919, "reputation": 63, "user_id": 4140146, "user_type": "registered", "accept_rate": 50, "profile_image": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/fa511d0c9ed6718cc0b51435eb2b488b?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2", "display_name": "innocent", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/4140146/innocent"}, "is_accepted": true, "score": 4, "last_activity_date": 1416584818, "last_edit_date": 1416584818, "creation_date": 1416573526, "answer_id": 27061604, "question_id": 27060751, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>Finally got it with some experimentation</p>\n\n<pre><code>context.getVariable(\"calloutResponse.status.code\");\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Cheers!!</p>\n"}, {"owner": {"account_id": 3872187, "reputation": 1207, "user_id": 3207199, "user_type": "registered", "accept_rate": 78, "profile_image": "https://i.sstatic.net/cwD96.jpg?s=256", "display_name": "Michael Bissell", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/3207199/michael-bissell"}, "is_accepted": false, "score": 0, "last_activity_date": 1416599592, "creation_date": 1416599592, "answer_id": 27069227, "question_id": 27060751, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>Your the response object is defined in the Callout policy -- by default ApigeeUI uses calloutResponse, but good convention is to rename it to something more informative and less likely to get overwritten. </p>\n\n<p>So, if you named it, for example, \"yahooWeather\" you could then access the variable \"yahooWeather.status.code\".  </p>\n"}], "has_more": false, "quota_max": 300, "quota_remaining": 260}